<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
        COMPLETE the federation_modules seed so the DB-driven dynamic manifest
        (GET /api/federation/manifest) is AUTHORITATIVE for the host's remote
        topology — it no longer omits remotes the host's bundled static manifest
        (hugmesh.net src/assets/federation.manifest{,.prod}.json) carries.

        BACKGROUND. The host now resolves remotes DYNAMIC-FIRST (federation-api),
        with the bundled static manifest as a UNION FLOOR (hugmesh.net PR
        #78): on a successful authenticated DB read the host returns
        { ...staticFloor, ...dynamic } — the floor always present, the dynamic
        overlay overriding/adding slugs. Until the seed is complete the floor was
        the ONLY thing saving the remotes the DB omitted. The static manifest
        lists 7 slugs: login, matrix, mastodon, admin, mod, user, apidocs. The DB
        already seeds login (010-2), admin (010-2), matrix (024), mastodon (023)
        — plus host/remote-fragment/forum/games/wiki. The THREE static slugs with
        NO registry row were: mod, user, apidocs. This changeset adds them so an
        authenticated dynamic fetch is a full superset of the static floor (which
        then becomes a harmless union, shrinkable to host+login in a SEPARATE
        host-only follow-up — NOT this PR).

        PER-REMOTE visibility / requiresRole — MATCHED to the host's actual route
        gating (hugmesh.net src/app/app.routes.ts REMOTE_ROUTES + the
        canActivate guards in src/app/guards/*), NOT guessed:

          • mod     — REMOTE_ROUTES '/mod' is canActivate:[modGuard]; modGuard
                      requires session.isMod() (Casdoor 'mod' role), else /login.
                      The manifest visibility cut is BINARY (public=everyone vs
                      internal=ADMIN/INTERNAL-only, per ManifestService.isVisibleTo
                      + canSeeInternal) — there is NO "mod-or-above" tier, and a
                      plain MOD is NOT ROLE_ADMIN. Marking 'mod' internal would
                      therefore WRONGLY HIDE the mod console from a mod's own
                      authoritative dynamic manifest (it would survive only on the
                      shrinkable static floor), defeating this PR's "make the DB
                      authoritative" goal — exactly the reasoning that put 'user'
                      at 'public' below. So 'mod' is -> visibility='public'. Host
                      gating stays with modGuard + BFF authz (the manifest is NOT
                      the authz boundary; listing a public entry URL is not an
                      authz weakening — same as user/matrix/mastodon). KEEP
                      metadata.requiresRole='mod' (bare label, mirroring admin's
                      'admin' / forum's 'forum'): it remains a host gating hint AND
                      keeps the row scope=role-KILL-targetable (isSuppressedByScope
                      matches on metadata.requiresRole, independent of visibility).
                      mountAt '/mod'.

          • apidocs — REMOTE_ROUTES 'admin/docs' is canActivate:[adminGuard] (the
                      SAME guard as '/admin'); the route doc states "the admin-only
                      API-docs console (/admin/docs) need the admin role".
                      ROLE-GATED on ADMIN -> visibility='internal' +
                      metadata.requiresRole='admin' (same gate as the admin
                      console). mountAt '/admin/docs' (the more-specific path the
                      host registers before '/admin').

          • user    — REMOTE_ROUTES '/user' is canActivate:[userGuard]; userGuard
                      returns true for session.isUser() — i.e. ANY authenticated
                      identity (the route doc: "User is any authenticated
                      identity"); it ONLY bounces anonymous visitors to /login. It
                      is also the DEFAULT role-home landing for plain users
                      (roleHomeGuard: user -> /user). So it is NOT admin-restricted
                      and MUST appear in a plain ROLE_USER's authenticated manifest
                      (the manifest is fetched WITH the user's bearer;
                      anonymous/pre-login callers get a 401 and fall back to the
                      static floor, never this dynamic row). The manifest
                      visibility model is binary (public=everyone vs
                      internal=admin/internal-only) with no "authenticated but not
                      admin" tier, so marking 'user' internal would WRONGLY hide a
                      plain user's own role-home from their dynamic manifest. Host
                      gating is done by the route guards + BFF authz, NOT by
                      manifest presence, so listing the public entry URL is not an
                      authz weakening. -> visibility='public', NO requiresRole.
                      mountAt '/user' retained as a host rendering hint.

        remote_entry_url for each row matches the static manifest's CONTRACT
        (slug -> remoteEntry URL): the static dev/prod files use per-deployment
        URLs (localhost:420x dev / path-based prod), so — exactly like 022-025/028
        — these rows carry the platform service-DNS placeholder
        http://snapdragon-<slug>-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json that the deployment's
        per-remote Service wires; the dynamic overlay then OVERRIDES the static
        floor's URL for that slug at runtime. exposed_module './routes' matches
        every other remote-shell row (LOGIN/ADMIN/MOD/USER/API_DOCS_ROUTES are all
        exposed as './routes' per app.routes.ts).

        Each INSERT is guarded by an idempotent slug-absent MARK_RAN preCondition
        (the 022/023/024/025/028/010-2 pattern) so re-running over an existing DB —
        or one already partially seeded — is a no-op. The ${json.type} clob/jsonb
        column round-trips as a String over r2dbc (same harness as 022-028).
    -->

    <changeSet id="029-1-register-mod-module" author="federation">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules WHERE slug = 'mod'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <insert tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="slug" value="mod"/>
            <column name="display_name" value="Moderator Console"/>
            <column name="kind" value="remote-shell"/>
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://snapdragon-mod-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="exposed_module" value="./routes"/>
            <column name="version" value="0.1.0"/>
            <column name="visibility" value="public"/>
            <column name="enabled" valueBoolean="true"/>
            <column name="circuit_state" value="closed"/>
            <column name="metadata" value="{&quot;requiresRole&quot;:&quot;mod&quot;,&quot;mountAt&quot;:&quot;/mod&quot;}"/>
        </insert>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="029-2-register-apidocs-module" author="federation">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules WHERE slug = 'apidocs'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <insert tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="slug" value="apidocs"/>
            <column name="display_name" value="API Docs Console"/>
            <column name="kind" value="remote-shell"/>
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://snapdragon-api-docs:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="exposed_module" value="./routes"/>
            <column name="version" value="0.1.0"/>
            <column name="visibility" value="internal"/>
            <column name="enabled" valueBoolean="true"/>
            <column name="circuit_state" value="closed"/>
            <column name="metadata" value="{&quot;requiresRole&quot;:&quot;admin&quot;,&quot;mountAt&quot;:&quot;/admin/docs&quot;}"/>
        </insert>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="029-3-register-user-module" author="federation">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules WHERE slug = 'user'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <insert tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="slug" value="user"/>
            <column name="display_name" value="User Console"/>
            <column name="kind" value="remote-shell"/>
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://snapdragon-user-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="exposed_module" value="./routes"/>
            <column name="version" value="0.1.0"/>
            <column name="visibility" value="public"/>
            <column name="enabled" valueBoolean="true"/>
            <column name="circuit_state" value="closed"/>
            <column name="metadata" value="{&quot;mountAt&quot;:&quot;/user&quot;}"/>
        </insert>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
